      "file": "is-real-estate-a-good-career-in-india-proof.webp",
      "mobile": "is-real-estate-a-good-career-in-india-proof-mobile.webp",
      "alt": "Key figures for Is Real Estate, with article context.",
      "caption": "Figures and their source notes.",
      "heading": "Total Education Cost for Is Real Estate",
      "content": {
        "kind": "bundle",
        "sourceNeedCount": 3,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "needId": "proof:2",
            "type": "proof",
            "heading": "Commission Income, with the Lumps Shown",
            "kind": "items",
            "sourceSectionId": "income-reality",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 2,
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Tax on your own earnings comes after that."
              }
            ],
            "supporting": [
              "If the usual 1% is paid by one side on an Rs 80 lakh flat, the fee is Rs 80,000. GST at 18% is added to your invoice and goes to the government. It is not your income. Tax on your own earnings comes after that.",
              "Say two months of calls, visits and follow-up end in zero closings, and the third month brings one Rs 80,000 fee. Spread over three months that is about Rs 26,700 a month. The work was steady. The pay was not."
            ]
          },
          {
            "needId": "proof:6",
            "type": "proof",
            "heading": "Fraud, Fake Listings and Cash Deals",
            "kind": "figures",
            "figures": [
              {
                "value": "₹20,000",
                "label": "Typical Salary Range",
                "source": "Cash and black money. Income tax law limits cash: an advance of Rs 20,000 or more for a property transfer and a receipt of Rs 2 lakh or more both fall under cash restrictions, with a penalty equal to the amount. These limits are described under the Income-tax Act, 1961, and the new Income-tax Act, 2025 has applied since 1 April 2026 with renumbered sections, so confirm the current section with a tax professional.",
                "text": "Cash and black money. Income tax law limits cash: an advance of Rs 20,000 or more for a property transfer and a receipt of Rs 2 lakh or more both fall under cash restrictions, with a penalty equal to the amount. These limits are described under the Income-tax Act, 1961, and the new Income-tax Act, 2025 has applied since 1 April 2026 with renumbered sections, so confirm the current section with a tax professional."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "trust-risk",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 6,
            "supporting": [
              "Hyderabad police filed a report in January 2026 on pre-launch offer fraud. A Square Yards article describing it puts losses at about Rs 3,000 crore across about 2,500 victims, with 19 cases charge-sheeted.",
              "In August 2025 a Hyderabad owner lost Rs 12,75,711 after a caller posing as an NSG commando offered an advance rent, as reported by PTI. Owners who advertise online are targets too.",
